{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Louvre closed its doors to us today, the last night before the living artists take over. It was strange, walking through that silence with Raumer and Panofka, knowing the walls belong to history now, not just the present. I saw Alzire and L’École des maris earlier; Mlle Mars is still magnificent, though time has added a weight to her voice that suits the tragedy.\n\nI find myself thinking of our sons. I hope they are not merely playing at freedom, but learning the discipline that makes judgment possible. A child who is not taught to obey will never know the true dignity of doing what is right. I miss our evenings, the cards, the quiet. The air here is thick with expectation, but I am tired.\n\nTell the boys their father is well, and that he loves them.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080674,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":187,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1139,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-1SFNy9uLV3w2lju6ZuREFIB5GELdkKsL","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":1015.489,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0666901260504202,"prompt_per_second":937.4793818544563,"predicted_n":187,"predicted_ms":4449.316,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.92105376344086,"predicted_per_second":41.80417844001191}}